By Observation~\ref{o-c-all-kr-mono}, complete bipartite graphs have to be monochromatic if each partition class is large enough. 
For the following results we modify the constructions in the case of non-bipartite graphs with bounded radius and diameter. The general idea is the following. 
We transform all cliques into bicliques such that a vertex $v$ in the original graph $G$ corresponds to two new vertices $v_1, v_2$ in the new graph $G'$. 

