codex
The cleanest viable route is emerging from Theorem 23, not from a generic planted cut. Its reduction gives a native bounded-radius bipartite graph whose maximum matching cut is certified by an exact 3-cover, and the certificate can be compressed to the selected \(K_{3,3}\)-gadget IDs. I’m stress-testing a regular “layered” exact-cover distribution now; the key question is whether Algorithm X remains mechanically expensive while the intended invariant stays under the no-tool operation cap.
