codex
The concurrent cyclic-layer construction passes its static review and fixes the earlier “plant looks denser” flaw: every gadget lies in one of several identically generated full covers, all element degrees are equal, and the target layer is selected uniformly only after shuffling. The full self-test is still running; its dominant cost is the mandated 200,000 structure-aware samples plus repeated exact graph-template verification.
