The full audit exposed another important distinction: blind minimum-column Algorithm X can spend a long time on these cyclic layers, while the tag-bucketing algorithm succeeds immediately. I’m recording that honestly as Track B: the successful reference will be “tag bucketing + exact-cover verification,” and a capped blind Algorithm X run will remain a failing adversary with its node cost reported—not be mislabeled as the successful reference.
